{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EXIF Image File Directory.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EXIF Image File Directory.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"exif image file directory exif image file directory","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EXIF Image File Directory.md","fileName":"EXIF Image File Directory.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EXIF Image File Directory","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Image Metadata and JPEG Signatures]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Metadata and JPEG Signatures","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EXIF Image File Directory.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EXIF Image File Directory.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"exif image file directory exif image file directory","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EXIF Image File Directory.md","fileName":"EXIF Image File Directory.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EXIF Image File Directory","heading":"EXIF Image File Directory","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An EXIF image file directory groups related metadata fields within a JPEG or TIFF structure. Typical directories describe the primary image, camera and exposure information, interoperability fields, the embedded thumbnail, and GPS coordinates.\n\nThe directory structure matters because metadata are not merely a flat list of labels. Fields can point to related records and previews, allowing an analyst to compare values produced at different stages of capture and storage. Broken relationships or incompatible entries can indicate that a file was altered or rebuilt by other software.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Metadata and JPEG Signatures","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EXIF Image